WEBVTT

00:12:00.954 --> 00:12:03.121
The fear that I'm going to
put myself out there

00:12:03.537 --> 00:12:07.079
and I'm going to find myself experiencing,
you know,

00:12:07.079 --> 00:12:08.162
the definition we use it for,

00:12:08.162 --> 00:12:13.162
shame is the incredibly painful
experience of believing

00:12:13.496 --> 00:12:15.496
or feeling that we are unworthy,

00:12:15.996 --> 00:12:18.746
that we're flawed and unworthy of love
and belonging and connection.

00:12:18.746 --> 00:12:23.454
And so you can see how vulnerability
is a really big ask.

00:12:24.329 --> 00:12:26.121
It's a really big ask you.

00:12:26.246 --> 00:12:29.621
It's so interesting. Your analysis
reminds me of the Boston

00:12:29.621 --> 00:12:34.329
and Vandeleur work on precarious manhood,
which it basically says, look,